// Retire MCP runtimes (the agentmemory shim) after 30 minutes without use.
// Why: since the Max lane (2026-11-16) main runs on claude-cli, and each isolated heartbeat run opens
// a session-scoped MCP runtime. Such runtimes live until session reset or deletion, a config change
// or Gateway shutdown, and an isolated heartbeat session gets none of those. So every hourly heartbeat
// left two agentmemory shims and their process-group anchors behind: 20 processes, 1.46 GB by 11:45 on
// 2026-11-17, growing about 290 MB an hour. OpenClaw docs: gateway/config-extensions.md, "mcp".
// Cost: the first turn in a session after 30 quiet minutes reconnects the shim. Data is unaffected:
// the shim only proxies to the agentmemory service on 127.0.0.1:47300.
// Undo: `config unset mcp.sessionIdleTtlMs` (back to no idle eviction).
{
  mcp: {
    sessionIdleTtlMs: 1800000,
  },
}
